\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Cost-accuracy Pareto frontier re-costed on cloud GPU (single V100 at \$1.24/hr). Same X-axis definition, same Y-axis, same models. The cost of every FM point shifts ${\sim }10$--$100\times $ rightward relative to Figure~\ref {fig:pareto_hw}, and the cost of every \textsc  {lgbm}{} point shifts roughly $3\times $ rightward. On this figure, some of the larger FMs (Chronos-2, Moirai~2.0, TimesFM~2.5) that are not in Figure~\ref {fig:pareto_hw} become plottable because cloud-GPU numbers for them are published in A02, A06, and A04.}}{45}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
